            <h2>Route Introduction</h2>
            <p>The journey from Cincinnati, Ohio, to Bonaire bridges the rolling hills of the Ohio River Valley with the sun-drenched shores of the southern Caribbean. This route links Cincinnati/Northern Kentucky International Airport (CVG) with Flamingo International Airport (BON), delivering Midwestern travelers to an island celebrated for its underwater wonders and relaxed Dutch-Caribbean atmosphere.</p>

            <p>Bonaire distinguishes itself from typical Caribbean hotspots through an unwavering dedication to environmental preservation. The entire coastline surrounding the island functions as a protected marine park, drawing visitors who value sustainability alongside recreation. No high-rise resorts dominate the skyline; instead, low-rise developments blend into the arid landscape of cacti, divi-divi trees, and salt flats tinged pink by resident flamingo colonies.</p>

            <p>Every itinerary between these points demands at least one aircraft change. No carrier bridges the roughly 2,100-mile gap without touching down at an intermediate hub. The total time aloft and on the ground typically stretches from seven to twelve hours, shaped largely by where that connection occurs and how long layovers last.</p>
            <h3>Who Makes This Journey?</h3>
            <p>The passenger manifest reveals a character unlike routes to Cancun or Punta Cana:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Dedicated divers carrying their own regulators, BCDs, and wetsuits toward shore dives accessible directly from the beach</li>
                <li>Underwater photographers chasing crystal visibility that regularly exceeds 100 feet</li>
                <li>Windsurfing devotees seeking the steady trade winds that sweep across Lac Bay</li>
                <li>Birding enthusiasts scanning the Pekelmeer sanctuary for roseate spoonbills and Caribbean parakeets</li>
                <li>Families escaping Midwestern winters for dry warmth where humidity stays manageable</li>
                <li>Cruise extenders tacking on land-based exploration before or after sailing the ABC islands</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Essential Route Data:</h3>

