            <p>The absence of nonstop service reflects Bonaire's niche appeal rather than any infrastructure limitation. Flamingo International handles modern jet traffic comfortably, but the island's small scale and specialized tourism market don't generate the volume needed to sustain direct Midwestern links. Savvy travelers view the mandatory connection as an opportunity to stretch their legs and refresh before the final Caribbean hop.</p>

            <h2>Popular Airlines on This Route</h2>
            <p>Carriers serving this corridor fall into distinct categories, each offering different value propositions for the Bonaire-bound traveler.</p>
            <h3>Full-Service Carriers</h3>
            <h4>American Airlines</h4>
            <p>American dominates this market through its Miami fortress hub, the closest major US gateway to Bonaire.</p>
            <b>What sets Americans apart:</b>
            <ul>
                <li>Multiple daily departures from CVG to Miami, ensuring connection flexibility</li>
                <li>The Miami-Bonaire segment operates on dependable Boeing 737-800 equipment</li>
                <li>AAdvantage program delivers meaningful earning opportunities on both legs</li>
                <li>Admirals Club access in Miami eases layover waits for premium passengers</li>
                <li>Seasonal Saturday-only Charlotte connections supplement the Miami routing</li>
            </ul>
            <h4>Delta Air Lines</h4>
            <p>Delta leverages its Atlanta megahub to capture Cincinnati travelers seeking reliability and schedule consistency.</p>
            <b>Distinctive advantages:</b>
            <ul>
                <li>Atlanta-Bonaire service runs on dependable daily schedules</li>
                <li>The CVG-Atlanta hop is brief, minimizing exposure to domestic delays</li>
                <li>SkyMiles members enjoy broad redemption possibilities across the Caribbean</li>
                <li>Delta's operational excellence translates to fewer misconnections</li>
                <li>Airbus A319 or Boeing 737-700 typically handles the island segment</li>
            </ul>
            <h4>United Airlines</h4>
            <p>United funnels Cincinnati passengers through Houston Intercontinental, offering a western alternative to the Miami and Atlanta corridors.</p>
            <b>Notable features:</b>
            <ul>
                <li>Houston-Bonaire represents United's dedicated Caribbean service</li>
                <li>Star Alliance connectivity benefits MileagePlus members</li>
                <li>Polaris lounges in Houston provide a premium ground experience</li>
                <li>Generous policies toward sporting equipment benefit divers</li>
                <li>Seasonal Newark connections expand options for northeastern Ohio travelers</li>
            </ul>
            <h4>JetBlue Airways</h4>
            <p>The newest entrant to this market, JetBlue, commenced Bonaire service in late 2024, injecting fresh competition.</p>
            <b>Why JetBlue matters:</b>
            <ul>
                <li>Fort Lauderdale positioning offers competitive pricing</li>
                <li>Industry-leading legroom in standard economy cabins</li>
                <li>Complimentary high-speed Wi-Fi on every aircraft</li>
                <li>Free snacks and soft drinks distinguish the onboard experience</li>
                <li>TrueBlue points pool among family members</li>
            </ul>
            <h4>KLM Royal Dutch Airlines</h4>
            <p>KLM provides an intriguing transatlantic twist, connecting through Amsterdam before doubling back across the Atlantic.</p>
            <b>When KLM makes sense:</b>
            <ul>
                <li>Amsterdam-Bonaire operates on wide-body comfort</li>
                <li>Delta codeshares from CVG create seamless booking</li>
                <li>European stopover possibilities for multi-destination trips</li>
                <li>Traditional Dutch hospitality standards</li>
                <li>Superior baggage allowances compared to US peers</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Regional and Inter-Island Operators</h3>
            <h4>Divi Divi Air</h4>
            <p>This Bonaire-based carrier specializes in short hops to neighboring Curacao, enabling island combinations.</p>

